From e62c2ebc91d9fde102212143fe0b76380d9e5664 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Foreman <derek.foreman@collabora.com>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 14:12:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] surface-state: Fix assert firing when subsurfaces have no
 views

I've not been able to reproduce this, but have a report that this fires
when running Chromium on aarch64.

It seems plausible that we can get here when none of the subsurfaces have
views, and thus the flag won't be set.

Let's make the assert conditional on having views.

Fixes 6a280a8f
Fixes #1117

Signed-off-by: Derek Foreman <derek.foreman@collabora.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/weston/-/commit/f3e30e4692f02f3d6183a3c88b5ac59c9a8b610a]
---
 libweston/surface-state.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libweston/surface-state.c b/libweston/surface-state.c
index 3c31a0a..594e5f8 100644
--- a/libweston/surface-state.c
+++ b/libweston/surface-state.c
@@ -279,7 +279,8 @@ weston_surface_apply_subsurface_order(struct weston_surface *surface)
 		wl_list_for_each(view, &sub->surface->views, surface_link)
 			weston_view_geometry_dirty(view);
 	}
-	weston_assert_true(comp, comp->view_list_needs_rebuild);
+	if (!wl_list_empty(&surface->views))
+		weston_assert_true(comp, comp->view_list_needs_rebuild);
 }
 
 /* Translate pending damage in buffer co-ordinates to surface
-- 
